    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q_thaw": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I thaw the salmon?",
            "text": "<p>Move the fillets to the fridge the night before. Take them out of the packaging and pat them dry just before they go into the pan.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_done": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is 120&ndash;125&deg;F done?",
            "text": "<p>It gives the silky, medium center Miriam pulls her salmon at, when it just flakes at the thickest part. The FDA conservatively suggests cooking fish to an internal temperature of 145&deg;F, so poach it a few minutes longer if you prefer it cooked through. Eating raw or undercooked seafood may increase your risk of foodborne illness, especially with certain medical conditions.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_tear": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Why keep it below a simmer?",
            "text": "<p>A rolling boil tightens the outside before the center is ready. Small bubbles, the water barely shivering, cook it gently and evenly.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_ahead": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I make it ahead?",
            "text": "<p>Poach the salmon up to 2 days ahead and refrigerate it whole, then flake it just before serving. Keep the dressing separate until you eat, so the greens stay crisp.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_hold": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Warm or cold?",
            "text": "<p>Either. Flake it straight onto the salad while it is warm, or chill it for 20 minutes for a cold salad.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_sauce": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Do I need the eggs?",
            "text": "<p>No. They are optional, and the bowl works without them.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "q_thaw",
        "q_done",
        "q_tear",
        "q_ahead",
        "q_hold",
        "q_sauce"
      ],
